.SS CBOR_MEMBER
Makes the cbor::member entry of \f[CR]T::m\f[R] with the text of the
name \f[CR]m\f[R] as its key.
A type whose name holds a comma needs a type alias.
The errors of cbor::member apply.
.PP
\f[B]Parameters\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]T\f[R]: the type that holds the member
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]m\f[R]: the name of the member
.SS CBOR_DEFINE_TYPE_MEMBERS
Writes the cbor::describe_members specialization of \f[CR]T\f[R] with
the tag \f[CR]TAG\f[R] and one CBOR_MEMBER entry for each name in the
list.
The key of each member is its name.
The list takes up to 343 names.
The macro stands outside every namespace, after \f[CR]T\f[R].
A type whose name holds a comma needs a type alias.
The macro expands each name before it makes the key.
A name that is also an object\-like macro gives the key of what the
macro expands to.
A name that is not a member of \f[CR]T\f[R] does not compile.
A list of more than 343 names does not compile.
The errors of cbor::describe_members apply.
.PP
\f[B]Parameters\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]T\f[R]: the type to describe
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]TAG\f[R]: the tag of the type, or \f[CR]cbor::untagged\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]...\f[R]: the names of the members
.SS cbor::structs<T>
Writes a C++ value as CBOR and reads it back.
\f[CR]T\f[R], and each member of a struct in \f[CR]T\f[R], is one of the
types in this table.
\f[CR]encode\f[R] writes the item of the right column.
\f[CR]decode\f[R] takes only that item, under its own tag.
.PP
